{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared calendar week-start vectors. Read by coui_core",
    "(CoreCalendarGridData), coui_flutter (Calendar) and coui_web",
    "(Calendar) — a change to which weekday a week row starts on, or to",
    "how many days of the neighbouring months fill a grid, fails on every",
    "platform at once.",
    "",
    "Derived with Python's `datetime` (isoweekday: Monday 1 .. Sunday 7,",
    "the same numbering as Dart's `DateTime.weekday`), not with the Dart",
    "implementation under test.",
    "",
    "weekdayOrder: the weekday header, left to right, as DateTime weekday",
    "numbers, for a week that starts on `firstDayOfWeek`.",
    "",
    "cases: one month per weekday a month can start on, each laid out for",
    "a week starting on Sunday (the default), Monday and Saturday, plus a",
    "leap February and a December whose last week runs into the next year.",
    "`leading` is how many days of the previous month open the grid (also",
    "the column the 1st falls in); `dayNumbers` is the day of month in every",
    "cell, row by row; `firstCell` / `lastCell` are the first and last cell's",
    "dates (ISO). The grid is filled to whole weeks, so it has 4 to 6 rows."
  ],
